    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d616-a3">

                <pb facs="0641" n="529" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg529"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister for Foreign
                            Affairs to Ambassador Reid.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-05-11"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">May 11,
                    1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: I duly laid before the King, my
                    Sovereign, your note of the 7th instant, in which your excellency expresses the
                    Condolences of the President, Government, and people of the United States of
                    America on the occasion of the deeply lamented death of His Late Majesty King
                    Edward VII, and I have received the King’s commands to request your excellency
                    to convey to the President and Government of <pb facs="0642" n="530"
                        xml:id="pg530"/> the United States his most sincere thanks for their much
                    appreciated messages of sympathy in the great loss which has been sustained by
                    His Majesty, his royal house, and his subjects throughout the world.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Grey.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
